You are helping me finish setting up Notted, a Mac app that records my meetings and turns each one into a summary and a list of suggested tasks. Read this whole message, then talk with me to finish the setup.

## How Notted works

1. I record a meeting. Notted captures my microphone and the system audio, and keeps the recording on this Mac.
2. Notted transcribes the recording on this Mac, with no network.
3. I open one Claude Code session per meeting. It reads the transcript and writes the summary and the suggested tasks, following the instruction files described below.
4. When I say yes, the meeting is saved to my archive, a git folder.
5. I accept a suggestion to act on it. What accepting does comes from my instruction files.

